staurum wrote:

now as expected, i.e. the expectancy has failed.

Would anyone please give me some ideas as to what should have happened in order for the zone to succeed..... Please also don't tell me that the left shoulder up the top is the reason, because i do NOT believe it is.:)

@bro C: I'm asking for your favour here, I should be the one thanking you for your responses now, if you wouldnt' mind, if price is really going to C & D, what PA, do you think, that has given us a clue for that zone (redbox in line with C&D) to succeed? or if not yet happened, what do you expect to happen in order for us to have good reasons to trade the redbox? or are we just going to touchtrade it? Oh... btw, don't u think the UCAD failed zone is a bit similar to the EURNZD chart above? lol... just saying though. no need to respond to this:)

@bro A: I'd think it's good for you, first, to guess what the reasons are. To me, the levels where u added and got stopped provide me with another example of a "zone failure". If i may: you said "...I put SL beyond that BSZ was reacting to", my question would be: please describe in details the *reaction* you were looking for? It may help to advise ourself like "if the reaction does not suit my definition of reaction, then i would not want to trade". something like that. the statement: "how to manage LTF adds?" shows a little sign of "trying-to-find-trades" habit, and an insufficient understanding of the structure of your own trading strategy. (please forgive me if i'm wrong, i'm just sharing my opinion that results my past experiences)

